<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Objectives Resolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Objectives Resolution was adopted by the Constituent Assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> on 12 March 1949, under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaquat-ali-khan">Liaquat Ali Khan</a>. It declared that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> belongs to God and is exercised by the people through their representatives within limits set by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, while promising democracy and protection for minorities. It served as the preamble of Pakistan's constitutions and was made a substantive part of the constitution in 1985.</p></div>
